	abstract = {The work reported in this paper is a continuation of an experimental effort on unsteady laminar separation. In earlier reports the author discuss the problem of laminar separation over a curved surface with particular attention to the immediate neighborhood of separation. In the present paper the authors report on an extension of a work which includes detailed measurements near, as well as upstream and downstream of separation, all the way to the point of stagnation and beyond the downstream end of the body, into the wake. The data presented here therefore offer a complete and detailed picture of unsteady separating flow over a bluff body, readily available for comparison with numerical calculations.},
